  {
   "user": "Tim",
   "message": "- [4 — ring](https://discord.com/channels/1510645022645555321/1532914112693272657/1534878524773761045)\n    - obligations, traditions\n    - In piano playing, the ring finger (4, historically 3) is the second of the “weak fingers” and is anatomically attached to the middle finger, thus being built out of something legible; this finger is often used with finger 2 in playing thirds (a common interval in both melodies and harmonies) because they are balanced.",
   "timestamp": "2026-08-06T11:14:44.369000+00:00",
   "channel": "general",
   "channel_id": "discord:1532905838883242114",
   "thread": "five chats, five fingers",
