  {
   "user": "Tim",
   "message": "- [5 — pinky](https://discord.com/channels/1510645022645555321/1532914123132895313/1534878539789111316)\n    - structural extreme, boundaries, cutting, thin crust, outside reach\n    - In piano playing, the pinky finger (5, historically 4) is the third of the “weak fingers”, but is also often used for a fairly blunt sound (think of a karate chop) and also is used for playing intervals of an octave and beyond. Often used to double the note in the thumb, and also used for jumps to the low and high extremes.",
   "timestamp": "2026-08-06T11:14:51.796000+00:00",
   "channel": "general",
   "channel_id": "discord:1532905838883242114",
   "thread": "five chats, five fingers",
   "thread_id": "discord:1534879057693507654",
